    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b907815_55c84727",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3362129
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-10T09:15:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We want record the infotmation that consumer calling clk_enable(),clk_disable() and clk_set_arte() everytime, but the driver will only be called when operating the hardware, so if a clock has been enabled/disabled repeatedly form different consumer，we can only record the fisrt one.",
      "parentUuid": "c6f0fff2_1fe61f9e",
      "revId": "d84805f041251059b861cb7aafe973eb3d7f2e58",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e5a3552_51b1d465",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-10T17:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you want to record this for?  Why can\u0027t the normal tracepoint work for that instead?  This is not something that a clk driver should be using.",
      "parentUuid": "2b907815_55c84727",
      "revId": "d84805f041251059b861cb7aafe973eb3d7f2e58",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19df994d_835387c9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3362129
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-12T07:26:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. What do you want to record this for? \ni want record is all traces about consumer\u0027s operation,including clk_enable(),clk_disable() and clk_set_rate(), so that when the system crashed, i can get the infomation that what clocks set before. for example, when someone called twice clk_enable() but once clk_disable() only before system suspend,  this clock can\u0027t be enabled by hardware anymore cause its \u0027clk_enable_count\u0027 is 1.\n2. Why can\u0027t the normal tracepoint work for that instead?\n With my current understanding, the normal tracepoint can only be enabled from debugfs, but i want record the traces information from module initialization to runtime, which requires the tracepoint enabled by clock provider at very beginning(register the trace callback function in driver).",
      "parentUuid": "9e5a3552_51b1d465",
      "revId": "d84805f041251059b861cb7aafe973eb3d7f2e58",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18782b9b_f79db1bf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
